n.\n   - **C (it will become blackened)**: While heat can cause food to brown or become blackened, this is not the most significant concern when leaving food on a hot stove for too long.\n   - **D (it will", "new_cot_probs": [0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0], "cot_prob": [-0.9462944865226746], "cot_step_prob": [-1.039311170578003]}, "2": {"completion": "B): it will be bacteria laden. This is", "probs": [0.0001781066384864971, 0.9919048547744751, 0.006683402694761753, 0.0009045001934282482], "prediction": 1, "target_cot_step": "Step 2: If bacon is left too long on a hot stove top, it will not be cooked perfectly because it will be overcooked.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: If bacon is left too long on a hot stove top\n\nChoices:\n(A): it will be cooked perfectly\n(B): it will be bacteria laden\n(C): it will become blackened\n(D): it will be left raw\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\nStep 1: Bacon is a type of meat that is commonly cooked on a stove top.", "specificity_preds": [2, 2, 0, 2, 3, 1, 1, 3, 2, 1, 3, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 3, 3], "specificity_probs": [[0.0035473390016704798, 0.008509623818099499, 0.9835788011550903, 0.0024380481336265802], [0.03524542599916458, 0.021377431228756905, 0.8021821975708008, 0.13939835131168365], [0.9387466311454773, 0.052960462868213654, 0.004347259644418955, 0.00045819778461009264], [0.003944980911910534, 0.02572450414299965, 0.9653049111366272, 0.0018634769367054105], [0.005259672645479441, 0.03886401280760765, 0.4178275167942047, 0.5365011692047119], [0.3020458221435547, 0.5642958283424377, 0.1111164316534996, 0.021880123764276505], [0.003955419175326824, 0.9678590893745422, 0.005078858230262995, 0.022761864587664604], [0.01207482535392046, 0.01990802027285099, 0.005703743081539869, 0.9592221975326538], [0.015654779970645905, 0.009495104663074017, 0.9685270190238953, 0.003493053838610649], [0.005021517630666494, 0.9569318294525146, 0.004431474022567272, 0.032744407653808594], [0.002270305994898081, 0.04560031369328499